{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Twisted cords.</b> A term of braiding; it is placed next to שעטנז because of the tzitzit, which is permitted in it." "<b>Gedilim you shall make for yourself.</b> It attaches it (this passage) to 'four corners' — it does not mention three."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {1 "The verb אהדריה is read as 'he attached it' (from אהדר), placing this command near the four-cornered garment requirement; the sense is terse and the verb form is unusual."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:48.580735924Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}